---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = "MosleyOS Privacy Policy | Ovieh Mosley";
const description = "What MosleyOS stores, how it uses Google Calendar access, and how to have data deleted.";
const updated = "November 1, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} noindex>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <article class="app-page">
    <header class="app-header">
      <p class="eyebrow font-mono text-accent">// MOSLEYOS / PRIVACY</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta font-mono">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>
        MosleyOS is a private, invite-only family organizer run by Ovieh Mosley. This policy explains
        what the app stores, how it uses access to Google Calendar, and how to have data removed.
      </p>

      <h2>Who uses MosleyOS</h2>
      <p>
        Only invited adults can sign in. Children don't have accounts; an adult in the household can
        add a child's name, color, and notes so events can be assigned to them.
      </p>

      <h2>What MosleyOS stores</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your account email and the household you belong to.</li>
        <li>
          Household content you enter: member names and notes, calendar events, recipes, shopping
          lists, and details of documents you choose to keep in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you connect Google Calendar: the Google account's email address, the calendar you chose,
          the time zone used for events, and the IDs of the events MosleyOS created there.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data is kept on your household's devices and in the app's database and private file
        storage, hosted by Supabase. Only signed-in members of your household can access your
        household's data.
      </p>
      <p>
        MosleyOS does not use your device's GPS. Where a family member is likely to be is worked out
        only from their scheduled events.
      </p>

      <h2>Google Calendar access</h2>
      <p>
        The household owner can connect one Google account to copy the household's events to one
        Google Calendar. MosleyOS asks Google for permission to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>see the account's email address, to show which account is connected;</li>
        <li>list the calendars the account can use, so the owner can pick one;</li>
        <li>create, change, and delete events on the chosen calendar.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        MosleyOS uses this access only to keep that calendar matched to the household's MosleyOS
        events. The copy goes one way: MosleyOS does not read, store, or use other events or data in
        the Google account.
      </p>
      <p>
        The authorization Google issues is stored encrypted on the server and is never sent to
        anyone's phone. Disconnecting Google Calendar in the app deletes it and stops all further
        changes; events already copied stay in Google Calendar. You can also remove MosleyOS's access
        at any time from your
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account settings</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        MosleyOS's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>What MosleyOS doesn't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It doesn't sell, rent, or share your data with anyone.</li>
        <li>It doesn't show ads or use your data for advertising.</li>
        <li>It doesn't use Google data to train AI models.</li>
        <li>It doesn't include analytics or tracking.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The only outside services involved are the ones that run the app: Supabase (database,
        sign-in, and file storage) and, if you connect it, Google Calendar.
      </p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        Signing out clears MosleyOS data from that device. To delete your account or your household's
        data from the server, email <a href="mailto:mosley@ovieh.com">mosley@ovieh.com</a> and it
        will be removed within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new date. If MosleyOS
        starts using your data in a new way, households will be told before it happens.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Ovieh Mosley, <a href="mailto:mosley@ovieh.com">mosley@ovieh.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .app-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 1rem;
  }

  .app-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
</style>
